**Subject:** Automation update: November

Hi Patrick,

Here is a summary of where we got to with automation in November.

**Highlights**

- The Playwright pipeline is live. The multibranch job on Jenkins now runs the suite nightly on OpenShift, using the Playwright image with browsers built in and credentials mounted from the OpenShift secret.
- The ENTS regression pack finishes in 1 hour 26 minutes, against just over 10 hours on the legacy suite. That is between 5 and 7 times faster, depending on how the failed journeys are counted.
- ENTS coverage now reaches approval: we added [number] test cases that approve a submitted transfer in ENTS Core, so a transfer is checked from creation through to approval.

**Delivered this month**

- **Full regression run on Playwright.** 38 test cases across BISS, ENTS and the data step ran in 1 hour 37 minutes. 30 passed. The 8 failures are classified: 6 locator or timeout, 2 test data.
- **Runtime test data at scale.** The Test Data Vault handed out 189 herds in that run with none typed into a feature file. 4 unusable herds were marked bad and skipped automatically.
- **Self-healing measured.** The run recorded 129 rescues that would previously have been failures, mostly click fallbacks. One locator accounts for half of them, so we know where to fix first.
- **Progress dashboard for management.** A multi-metric comparison of the legacy suite, our modernised Selenium framework and Playwright, in HTML and PDF, built from measured run times and counted code metrics.
- **Framework showcase.** Three animated walkthroughs (architecture, how Playwright works inside the framework, and maintainability with runtime data) and a 45-minute session script covering the folder structure, CI/CD and a live demo.
- **Training plan.** An eight-week plan of 30-minute sessions for the ENTS and BISS testers, so the team can start a run and triage results without depending on one person.

**Plan for December**

- Fix the 8 failing test cases, starting with the three long BISS application journeys.
- Repair the document-type dropdown locator, which removes about half of the click fallbacks.
- Extend ENTS Core coverage beyond approval.
- Continue the remaining Staff packs (TC_28 to TC_37) on the shared step library.
- Start the training sessions and set up the weekly triage rota.

Happy to go through any of this in more detail, or to share the dashboard and the latest run report.

Thanks,
Aniket

